  "body": "## What changed\n\nA Contour on an open run of a part (an edge chain that does not close) no longer moves the tool centre along the run. The tool centre now stands one tool radius plus the stock to leave off the run, on the side that has no part material.\n\n- New `machining2d::contour_open_run` in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_run_side.rs`.\n  - It reads the part section at each cut level, 0.01 mm above the level.\n  - It tests two points 0.05 mm left and right of each run segment to find the side with material.\n  - It offsets the run to the other side (the air side) and cuts it with `contour_along_chain`.\n  - Climb keeps the material on the right of the tool (#1555). Conventional goes the other way.\n- It refuses the run by name in these conditions:\n  - The run has part material on both sides at a level.\n  - The material side changes between levels or along the run.\n  - The tool beside the run overlaps the part (for example, the run ends at a wall).\n  - The offset folds onto itself.\n- A run with no part material beside it at any level keeps the old centreline ride. The path note tells this.\n- `generate.rs` (Contour, selection arm) calls the new function when the picks are on a finished part (`part_solid`). Picks on the stock keep the old ride. The run's notes now go into the path (the `stitch` helper drops them).\n- `selection.rs`: the note for open runs now says \"Side does not apply to open runs - the tool stays on the run's air side, read from the part\".\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/1777-contour-open-run-side.md`.\n\nThe gouge gate is not changed. Before this fix, the post of the reported case was already blocked by the gouge gate. Now the program is correct, so the post is written.\n\n## Readings (block 40 x 40 x 10 at the origin, 10 mm end mill, Z 10 to 0)\n\n| Case | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| One open north edge, Side Auto / Inside / Outside | tool centre on y = 20; Gouge at moves 5, 6; post blocked (\"program cuts below the model in 512 cell(s), worst 10.00 mm\") | tool centre on y = 25; 0 warnings; post written (25 lines) |\n| North and east edges | post blocked (960 cells) | tool stays 5 mm off the block; 0 warnings; post written (33 lines) |\n| Closed rim | offset one radius out; post written | unchanged |\n| Open run with Boundary area controls | refused by name | unchanged |\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests:\n- `camcraft-motion` lib, `machining2d::contour_run_side::tests` (8 tests): `an_open_edge_is_cut_one_radius_off_on_its_air_side`, `stock_to_leave_moves_the_tool_further_off`, `conventional_travels_the_air_side_the_other_way`, `a_run_with_material_on_both_sides_is_refused`, `a_run_whose_sides_change_between_levels_is_refused`, `a_run_that_ends_at_a_wall_is_refused`, `a_run_with_no_material_beside_it_rides_its_line`, `a_degenerate_run_is_refused_not_ridden`.\n- `camcraft-app` new suite `contour_open_side`: `an_open_edge_of_a_part_is_cut_on_its_air_side_for_every_side`, `two_open_edges_turn_the_corner_on_their_air_side` (both also check that `posting::post_setup_unwritten` is Ok).\n- `camcraft-app` `operations`: `an_open_run_contours_on_its_centerline` is renamed `an_open_run_contours_on_its_air_side` and now checks the offset ends. `a_mixed_pick_list_cuts_boundary_then_run_and_says_what_overlap_means` now checks that the run gives no Gouge warning (before, it checked that the centreline gouge was flagged).\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` is green on a3367c834 (motion lib + 48 motion suites ok in 328 s, app lib + 119 app suites ok in 750 s, 0 failed). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\nNo golden CL or NC file and no snapshot PNG changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The maintainer's model `testdata/models/Block-w-slot.step` (not committed; the tests use the hand-built block of `area_support`).\n- The GUI. The viewport still draws the picked run (`chains_of`), not the offset ride. The toolpath preview shows the ride.\n- The Boundary errors of the report (open chain as Include, vertical face as a line). They belong to #1727 / PR #1756.\n- Open runs on tilted (3+2) setups: the code path is the same, but no test reads it.\n\n## Overlap\n\nThis PR changes one note string in `selection.rs`. PR #1769 also edits that file, so a small merge conflict is possible. This PR does not edit `contour_open.rs`, `stitch.rs`, `boundary*.rs` or `picks.rs` (PRs #1756, #1769, #1748). `offset_run` is copied from `contour_open.rs`; a follow-up can share it after #1756 merges.\n\nChangelog: Contour on an open edge of a part now cuts with the tool on the edge's air side (one radius off), instead of on the edge, and refuses a run with no clear air side by name (#1777)\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #1777\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
